                        "entry_id": "7eb5c6a1-9a3c-30b9-bc04-69fd59ace0cd",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Solingen (an independent city in North Rhine-Westphalia, in western Germany)"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "neuter",
                            "proper-noun"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "eb15aa95-c50b-4966-8126-5f98be55c9bb",
                                "sense_id": "d375a1a1-002a-3d69-86b6-429bbf3cb179",
                                "text": "Einige wollen behaupten, dasz die Urväter der jetzigen Fabrikanten aus Steyermark ins Herzogthum Berg gezogen, andere behaupten, dasz dieselben aus dem Elsasz dorthin gekommen seyen, woselbst ein Dorf befindlich ist, welches Sellingen [sic] heiszt, und wovon der Name Solingen seinen Ursprung habe.",
                                "translation": "Some people want to claim that the ancestors of the present manufacturers moved from Styria to the Duchy of Berg, others claim that the same came there from Alsace, where a village is located, which is called Sellingen [sic] and of which the name Solingen had its origin.",
                                "english": "Some people want to claim that the ancestors of the present manufacturers moved from Styria to the Duchy of Berg, others claim that the same came there from Alsace, where a village is located, which is called Sellingen [sic] and of which the name Solingen had its origin."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
